newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.misc

Hi, 

I am trying to use the pthreads library on axp-osf version 2.0.
I wrote a short test program attached.

A few problems occur during execution:

1) Even though "taskAttributes" is set to spawn "task" with a new priority,
the actual priority is that of "main".

2) pthread_setprio is not implemented apparently since we get the error
message: task: pthread_setprio error: Function not implemented

So how can I assign a priority to a thread ???

3) The "main" code seems to be considered as a thread (it has got an ID, etc. )
BUT, when its last instruction is reached, the program terminates even if the
"task" thread  hasn't executed. This motivates the infinite loop at the end.


What do you think about these problems ?

Are you aware of problems with this library in general ?

Thanks for your help,

Alex

---------------------------------------------------------------------

#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <errno.h>

pthread_startroutine_t task()
{
    printf("task: my prio is: %d\n", pthread_getprio(pthread_self()));

    if ( pthread_setprio(pthread_self(), PRI_FG_MAX_NP) == -1 )
	perror("task: pthread_setprio error");

    return (pthread_startroutine_t)0;
}


int main(int argc, char **argv)
{
    pthread_t threadID;
    pthread_addr_t dummy;
    pthread_attr_t taskAttributes;
    

    if ( pthread_attr_create(&taskAttributes) == -1 )
	perror("main: pthread_attr_create");

    if ( pthread_attr_setprio(&taskAttributes, PRI_FG_MAX_NP) == -1 ) 
	perror("main: pthread_attr_setprio error");

    pthread_create(&threadID, taskAttributes, 
		   (pthread_startroutine_t)task,
		   dummy);


    printf("\n");

#if 1
    while (1) {}
#endif


    printf("main here\n");

    return 0;
}
----------------------------------------------------------------------




