I did a little experiment this afternoon.  I created a file system
on an ULTRIX V4.4 system, populated it and generated a list of
checksums.  I then moved the file system to an OSF/1 V1.3 system
ran fsck and generated the same checksum list.  I also added a
directory of a few MB of files (the V1.3 root file system).

I moved the file system back to ULTRIX, ran fsck (no complaints)
and compared the checksum listings; no differences.  I was also
able to read all the new OSF/1 files.

This was only a test between ULTRIX V4.4 and OSF/1 V1.3 (three
versions old now).  Unless the CSC or engineering group were
to give it their blessing, I doubt it would be supported, but
it does seem to work.

Take that for what little it is worth...

