We are using it on SGIs. It certainly run windows *MUCH* faster than other PC emulators that I have seen on site. It has certainly allowed me to run a powerful word processor much faster than any UNIX "native" ones that I have tried before.

The version that we have is still a 286 emulation, which starts to be a pain, as more and more new products requires a 386 as a minimal machine. I understand that a 386 version is been worked on.

Problems? if one want to list the content of a unix directory from any of the windows applications, one has to be veeeerrrry patient while softwindows goes pulling the information. Also, a couple of times, my "PC disk" was corrupted without apparent reason, forcing me to re-install all my PC applications. (Since then, I have backups... but have not yet had a "chance" to use them). At last, once you start using windows, forget about spare cpu cycles on the SGI; but this is more a "Windows" problem than a softwindow one (also, there is a setting that makes softwindow idle when there is no activity in it. However, some of my colleagues told me about some problems that might happen if one uses this setting. I am afraid that I do not recall exactly what).

Altogether a useful product, but be prepared to suffer from time to time.
