X-Deja-AN: 100926885
organization: National Center for Atmospheric Research/Boulder, CO
newsgroups: comp.soft-sys.dce,comp.unix.osf.misc

Environment: DEC Alpha OSF/1, DCE 1.0.3

We are having an annoying problem with one of our DCE client programs.
It uses DCE pipes to send the stdout and stderr (with two threads) back
to a remote program acting as the DCE server (but was a client to initiate
the request).

We are getting what appears to be random segmentation violations, most often
in the thread management code, while deep inside an RPC call.  I suspect that
we are somehow either trashing memory or using some DCE routine wrong.

Question: Is there any way to turn on any consistency checking of the
thread management data structures or validity checking of the routine
arguments?

The coder is turning blue trying to find the problem, and we don't have
the time yet to turn someone else loose in an in depth static evaulation
of the code. :-(

We also appear to have the problem on SGI Irix 5.3 and DCE 1.0.2 beta code.

